parameters.description:
(Conditional) The existing Service ID for a Service Transfer. Send the whole AVC # (e.g. AVC000000000000) or only the last 5 digits (e.g 00000). You can send `serviceRef` instead.

It is required for Service Transfer orders, and relevant to them only.

Send `customer_authority_date` with it. A `service_ref` without one is rejected with a 400.

If you send it, the response shows the matching resource in `serviceIDMatch`. That is on the copper line resources (FTTB / FTTN / FTTC) or on the NTD's `uniPortD` ports (FTTP / HFC / Fixed Wireless). Exactly one carries `true` when the AVC validates.

Problems validating the Service ID match appear in the `siteRestrictionError` object on the `siteRestriction`. They include:

 - RJ002003 - The provided AVC does not exist: {AVC}
 - RJ002004 - The provided AVC has recently been disconnected: {AVC}
 - RJ002005 - The provided AVC exists at a different location: {AVC}
 - RJ002006 - The provided AVC has recently been disconnected at a different location: {AVC}

NbnSiteRestrictionError.description:
nbn's refusal of a qualification item, as nbn sends it. On a Service Transfer check, the reason the `serviceRef` did not validate:

 - RJ002003 - The provided AVC does not exist: {AVC}
 - RJ002004 - The provided AVC has recently been disconnected: {AVC}
 - RJ002005 - The provided AVC exists at a different location: {AVC}
 - RJ002006 - The provided AVC has recently been disconnected at a different location: {AVC}
